   "ocr_text": "BACK-TO-WORK Pumping Checklist\nA simple one-page plan for\nyour workdaypumping routine\nMomcozy x Aeroflow Breastpumps | Melissa Kotlen, RN, IBCLC |\nSarah Van Zandt, IBCLC, PMH-C\nl. Before Your First Day Back\n3. Have A Backup Plan\nTest your pumping setup before the first\nworkweek.\nO Know one backup option ifyour pump\ndoes not cooperate.\nConsider hand expression or a backup\nmanual pump.\nKeep extra pump parts at work or in\nyour bag.\nCarry a spare charger or power cord.\nIf safe milk storage is not available,\nO keep prioritizing comfort and regular\nmilk removal.\nO Confirm that pumping feels comfortable\nand your flange fit works foryou.\nO Knowyour pump parts, charger/power\nsource, and basic setup.\nO Identify when and where you can\nrealistically pump during your workday.\nO Plan around your baby's usual feeding\npattern, your time apart, and your\navailable work breaks.\nO Check what workplace pumping\nprotections and space may apply to you.\n2. Pack Your Pump-At-Work Bag\n4. Keep The Routine Flexible\nPump + charger or power source\nO Correct-fit flanges or inserts\nO Bottles or milk storage bags\nO Cooler bag + frozen ice packs, if needed\nO Spare parts for the pieces most likely to\nget lost or fail\nAim for regular milk removal-not\nperfect timing.\nIf baby feeds before you leave, adjust\nthe timing of your first pump.\nIf meetings or breaks shift, adjust the\nremaining sessions as needed.\nA shorter session can still provide some\nmilk removal and relief when time is\nlimited.\nO Labels or a simple tracking system\nNursing pads + an extra shirt\nO Water + snack\nO Avoid making skipped milk removals\nyour regular pattern.\nKeep it simple: the best routine is oneyou can actually repeat on a real workday.\nPlanning aid based on the Momcozy x Aeroflow Breast Pumps Webinar. Individual routines and needsvary.\nmomcozy i AeroflowOBreastpumps",
